-- check/bad (core): a `pub compare` makes the `foreign type` of its module
-- orderable only when it is THAT type's compare (A.54).
--
-- A module's `pub` values are one namespace (§11), so "does this module
-- declare a `compare`?" is not the same question as "does this foreign type
-- have one". `Tag`'s `compare` is here, `Handle`'s is not, and the gate read
-- the module: the tuple below derived an ordering whose first part was a
-- call to `compare` with a `Handle` in hand — no diagnostic, and an
-- unsound call in the dispatch table (`part 0 top compare`).
--
-- The receiver is a TUPLE and not a `Handle` so that the module rule of
-- §1.2, which answers `Handle`'s own `<` in step 2 of §6.3.1, cannot answer
-- this one: derivation over the shape is what consults the gate.
pub foreign type Handle


pub type Tag
    = Tag Int


pub compare : Tag, Tag -> Order
compare a b =
    LT


pub before : ( Handle, Int ), ( Handle, Int ) -> Bool
before a b =
    a < b
